    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0510" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/32649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-19T23:00:00-04:00">January 19,
                            1944—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. Your 83 of January 10, midnight. Should Hewitt still be in Stockholm, you are
                    instructed to inform him that Kersten’s proposition should not even be
                    considered. For Hewitt’s information the only terms which this Government is
                    prepared to give are those of unconditional surrender. The substance of this
                    “peace feeler” will be communicated to the British and Soviet Embassies
                        here.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d268-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
